{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015CMHcQvKenHfXgnGdtb3PJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator) by generating Go reimplementations of GNU utilities from formal specs, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline: extract (C source) → specify (human-authored PRDs/use cases) → synthesize (orchestrator generates Go) → verify (differential testing). Shared pkg/ (sys, format, testutils) supports cmd/ utility packages.\n\n**Current state:** Specifications exist through rel05.4. Code generation has progressed through several releases. On the current generation branch (`generation-gh-336-generate-code-r05.3`), Task 357 already committed uniq implementation (R1-R4).\n\n**Current release:** rel05.3 — sorted-stream comparison pair (uniq, comm). Uniq appears complete per commit history. Comm remains.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 05.3 has two use cases:\n- **rel05.3-uc001-uniq** — Task 357 committed (\"Implement cmd/uniq -- core line deduplication prd-uniq R1-R4\")\n- **rel05.3-uc002-comm** — not started, next in line\n\nComm is a straightforward sorted-file comparison utility. It reads two sorted files and produces three-column output (lines unique to file1, unique to file2, common). Flags suppress columns (-1, -2, -3) and control delimiter/order checking. This fits within a single task at 150-250 LOC.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/comm -- sorted file comparison (prd-comm R1-R4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd016-comm.yaml (comm PRD -- all requirements and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.3-uc002-comm.yaml (comm use case -- end-to-end execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.3.yaml (test suite -- expected inputs and outputs for comm)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern, SIGPIPE handling)\n      - cmd/uniq/main.go (sibling utility in same release -- reference for style and patterns)\n      - cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go (sibling test file -- reference for differential test structure)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/comm/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: comm utility implementation -- sorted file comparison with column suppression\n      - path: cmd/comm/comm_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gcomm reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement the comm command that reads two sorted files and produces\n          three-column output: lines unique to FILE1 (column 1), lines unique\n          to FILE2 (column 2), and lines common to both (column 3). Columns\n          are separated by a tab character by default. Each output line is\n          prefixed with the appropriate number of tab delimiters to indicate\n          its column. Match GNU comm behavior exactly under LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement column suppression flags: -1 suppresses column 1 (lines\n          unique to FILE1), -2 suppresses column 2 (lines unique to FILE2),\n          -3 suppresses column 3 (lines common to both). Flags can be\n          combined (e.g., -12 suppresses both columns 1 and 2, showing only\n          common lines). When columns are suppressed, remaining columns shift\n          left -- their tab prefix count decreases accordingly.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement --output-delimiter=STR to replace the default tab\n          delimiter between columns. Implement --check-order (default) to\n          verify input files are sorted and emit a diagnostic to stderr if\n          not. Implement --nocheck-order to skip sort-order validation.\n          Implement --total to append a summary line with counts per column.\n          Support - as a filename meaning stdin (only one file may be stdin).\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests comparing the Go binary against the\n          Homebrew gcomm reference binary. Cover: basic three-column output,\n          each suppression flag alone and in combination, --output-delimiter,\n          --check-order with unsorted input, --nocheck-order, --total,\n          stdin via -, empty files, files with no common lines, and identical\n          files. Use testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests. Skip\n          gracefully if gcomm is not in PATH.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Use the standard differential testing pattern from\n          ARCHITECTURE.yaml shared_protocols: BuildBinary for the Go binary,\n          exec.LookPath(\"gcomm\") for the reference, t.Skip if not found,\n          RunDiffTests with []testutils.DiffTest.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() per\n          the SIGPIPE handling shared protocol.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the Env field per\n          DD6 (locale handling deferred). String comparison uses simple\n          byte-order comparison, matching GNU comm behavior under LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Use flag parsing consistent with cmd/uniq and other sibling\n          utilities. Parse flags with the standard library flag package.\n          Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on error. Write diagnostics to stderr.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/comm/main.go compiles with no errors or lint warnings.\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          \"go test ./cmd/comm/...\" passes when gcomm is available in PATH.\n          Tests cover basic output, all suppression flag combinations,\n          --output-delimiter, --check-order, --nocheck-order, --total,\n          stdin via -, empty files, no-common-lines, and identical files.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when gcomm is not in PATH,\n          producing no failures.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          Output matches gcomm byte-for-byte on stdout and stderr for all\n          test inputs under LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Production code is under 250 lines. Total file count is 2 (main.go + comm_test.go).\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27537,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27537},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea7d80c8-1b9b-4a86-8127-a8e9c7ef7913","uuid":"9ca7869b-72f2-4fe3-8d6e-12dfa5cb69fa"}
